  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>trastuzumab_emtansine</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>L01FD03</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>two compartments, IV dosing <small>(PK_2C)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Chen SC et al. 2017</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>previously treated patients with HER2-positive advanced gastric cancer</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>trastuzumab emtansine</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_trastuzumab_emtansine/TrastuzumabEmtansine_Chen2017_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>linear clearance (CL)</td><td>0.79</td><td>L/day</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr><tr><td>volume of distribution in the central compartment (V c)</td><td>4.48</td><td>L</td><td><small>V1</small></td></tr><tr><td>distribution clearance (Q)</td><td>0.62</td><td>L/day</td><td><small>Q</small></td></tr><tr><td>volume of distribution in the peripheral compartment (V p)</td><td>1.49</td><td>L</td><td><small>V2</small></td></tr><tr><td>KM</td><td>1.63</td><td>μg/mL</td><td><small>Km</small></td></tr></table><h4>About trastuzumab_emtansine</h4><p>Ado-trastuzumab emtansine is an antibody-drug conjugate used to treat breast cancer. It is authorised in the European Union and is used in cancer care, though it carries a boxed warning.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3997863\">Wikidata Q3997863</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.TrastuzumabEmtansine\">TrastuzumabEmtansine</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>